sunxi_wdt: keep the watchdog running from probe until userspace takes over

Without a bootloader-armed watchdog, a hang between kernel start and the
first userspace open of /dev/watchdog needs a physical reset. With
WDOG_HW_RUNNING the watchdog core pings it until it is opened, bounded by
watchdog.open_timeout, so A/B boot counting can fall back automatically.

--- a/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
@@ -286,7 +286,16 @@
 
 	watchdog_set_drvdata(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, sunxi_wdt);
 
-	sunxi_wdt_stop(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
+	/*
+	 * U-Boot leaves the watchdog off, so a kernel or init hang before
+	 * userspace opens /dev/watchdog would wait for a manual reset. Run it
+	 * from probe instead: the watchdog core pings it until userspace takes
+	 * over, for at most CONFIG_WATCHDOG_OPEN_TIMEOUT seconds.
+	 */
+	err = sunxi_wdt_start(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
+	if (err)
+		return err;
+	set_bit(WDOG_HW_RUNNING, &sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev.status);
 
 	watchdog_stop_on_reboot(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
 	err = devm_watchdog_register_device(dev, &sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
